{{!-- A1, "List", on a tag archive: the newest post as a lead, the rest as the shared row.

	{{> "tag/a1" tagName=tag.name}}

	tagName   the subject, for the lead's eyebrow

The tag archive shares the Feed's `feed_layout` setting because a buyer picking "a wide row per
post" means it everywhere posts are listed — AND IT NOW SHARES THE ROW. The design drew a compact
row here with a 132px thumbnail on the right and the Feed's wide row on the Feed; one setting
drawing two rows is a difference a publication cannot account for, so `archive/list-row.hbs` is
the row on both. The lead story is still this Surface's own.

THE LEAD IS PAGE 1 ONLY. Its eyebrow says "Latest in Interviews", which is true of the newest
post in the tag and of nothing on page 2. Rather than print a lie or drop the eyebrow, later
pages run every post through the same row as the rest — the archive narrows to a list once the
reader has left the front of it, which is also what the reader asked for by paging.

PAGE WIDTH, not the design's 1120px column: the masthead, the tag strip and the pagination around
this list are all at page width, and the row it draws is the Feed's, which is too. --}}
<section
	id="posts"
	aria-label="{{t "Posts"}}"
	class="container pt-2">
	{{#foreach posts}}
		{{#if @first}}
			{{#match ../pagination.page 1}}
				{{> "tag/lead" tagName=../tagName}}
			{{else}}
				{{> "archive/list-row"}}
			{{/match}}
		{{else}}
			{{> "archive/list-row"}}
		{{/if}}
	{{else}}
		<p class="font-body text-muted py-11">{{t "Nothing filed under this tag yet."}}</p>
	{{/foreach}}
</section>
